"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+3 with tertiary pattern 4 (ISUP grade group 1), no extraprostatic extension, positive surgical margins, and no seminal vesicle invasion. The absence of lymph nodes removed and lymphovascular invasion was noted. Preoperative PSA was low at 0.2.\n\nCountervailing findings include the positive surgical margins and the lack of nodal sampling, which is noted as pNx, widening uncertainty regarding nodal status. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy difference is noted as the Gleason pattern and ISUP report are missing. The numeric horizon suggests a follow-up period of approximately 66 months without an event. Postoperative PSA and its trajectory are critical missing pieces of information that would significantly revise this assessment. Missing previous notes also limit the current certainty. The fixed estimated horizon is 66.14 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 39.68–92.60 months; its coverage has not been validated."
